{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat collab/yang-clojure/1794210794000-engineer-cc1-p1-assoc-stale-metadata.prompt.md; tail -n 100 collab/yang-clojure/1794210794000-engineer-cc1-p1-assoc-stale-metadata.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log; rg -n 'ba2deb73|pick-second|clojure -M:test|recover-rebuilt-packet' collab/yang-clojure/179421*\"","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-09 08:2x GMT (real header below)\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 1dccb4ae-0261-4e80-88ca-2a5b98bc4d8b\n\n# Task: close P1-4 — stale tracking metadata survives packet content replacement\n\nRole: VM Engineer (fourth provenance edge in this family; a targeted fix)\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: muse-wonder-1.0 | Assigned: 2026-11-09 | Status: active\n- EXECUTION CONSTRAINT: no ssh, no local slow tests; report the commands.\n\n## The verdict (read fully)\n\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794214000000-codex-cc1-regate.findings.md\n\n## The defect\n\nmacro.cljc:909 p-assoc replaces packet CONTENTS while retaining the original\nvector's metadata; recover-packet:887 then trusts that ::origin-of and bypasses\nlineage recovery. Executed repro (JVM, returns :ok but records wrong history):\n\n  (defmacro pick-second [a b]\n    (assoc a 0 (first b) 1 (first (rest b))))\n  (defmacro feed [x]\n    (yin/application (yin/variable 'pick-second)\n      [x (yin/application (yin/variable 'g) [(yin/literal 2)])]))\n  (defn f [y] y)\n  (defn g [y] y)\n  (feed (f 1))\n\nWrong: {[] [:retained [:source :program-in 0 0]]} (a's source)\nRight: the FEED expansion's origin.\n\n## Required correction (codex's words)\n\n\"Invalidate stale tracking metadata when packet contents change, then recover\nprovenance from the resulting packet's actual lineage - or refuse\nmissing/ambiguous provenance. Add this case as a regression.\"\n\n## Design consideration (address it in your report)\n\nThis is the FOURTH edge in one family (fabricated :constructed on reassembly;\n:origin-of breaking literal encoding; ambiguous row-level first-match; now stale\nmetadata surviving content replacement). Each prior fix patched one operation.\nIf there is a structurally sound invariant that makes every such edge impossible\n— e.g. tracking metadata is only valid for the exact vector object it was\nattached to and MUST be dropped by any operation that changes contents (assoc/\nconj/subvec on a packet), enforced at ONE choke point — implement that instead of\noperation-by-operation patches. State which you chose and why.\n\n## Where\n\nWorktree /tmp/cc1-p1 over f440a2fb (git fetch; reset to origin/callsite-\ncontract-clojure first — that tip now CONTAINS the previous fix). Keep\nuncommitted; report git diff --stat + the exact verification commands.\n\nBegin the final response exactly with Completed-GMT / Completed-Local.\nmuse: workspace root: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld (cwd default)\nmuse: workspace trust: trusted source=run-flag\nmuse: warning: rules file at /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/CLAUDE.md is ignored this session because AGENTS.md takes precedence in that directory; merge still-applicable guidance into AGENTS.md or remove one of the two files\nmuse: Skills: 39 loaded · 1 warning\nmuse:   `skills_catalog` was trimmed to fit its size limit (32 KB): 2 descriptions compacted, 0 skill ids omitted\nmuse:   Run `muse skills list --source all` for full diagnostics.\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-09 07:56:05 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-09 14:56:05 +0700\n\nP1-4 is fixed in `/tmp/cc1-p1`, uncommitted.\n\n**Base note:** `f440a2fb` is not present locally and fetching is barred (no ssh). The worktree therefore remains on `fa70516f` with the previous P1 fix already uncommitted in it. I built on that state rather than resetting and destroying it.\n\n**Design choice:** the structural invariant, not an `assoc`-only patch. In [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:884), tracking metadata is now valid only for the exact vector object it was attached to. Every content-changing prelude primitive (`assoc`, `conj`, `vec`) routes its result through the single choke point `recover-rebuilt-packet` at [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:903), which drops `::origin-of` before lineage recovery. Extractive primitives (`first`, `get`) return the very tagged object, so they alone still trust its metadata. A rebuilt packet is re-provenanced only from its actual root/rows lineage; if no lineage entry accounts for it, it carries no provenance and is refused downstream as `:missing-provenance` rather than relabelled. In the repro, `(assoc a 0 (first b) 1 (first (rest b)))` now recovers `b`'s rows object from lineage and records the feed expansion's origin instead of `a`'s stale `[:source :program-in 0 0]`.\n\n**Regression:** added the exact codex case as a new `testing` block in `p1-packet-provenance-test` at [clojure_callsite_test.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1130), asserting `:ok`, a retained feed-expansion origin, never the stale source admission, and full call-site coverage validation.\n\n**`git diff --stat`** (against `fa70516f`; includes the prior uncommitted P1 fix):\n\n```\n src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc           | 408 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------\n test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc | 145 +++++++++++++\n 2 files changed, 466 insertions(+), 87 deletions(-)\n```\n\nThis round's increment is only the choke-point routing/doc in `macro.cljc` and the one regression block. `git diff --check` passes.\n\n**Verification (not run locally, per the no-local-slow-tests constraint — for the orchestrator):**\n\n```bash\ncd /tmp/cc1-p1\nclojure -M:test -e \"(require 'yang.clojure-callsite-test 'yang.core.call-test 'yin.vm.encoder-test) (let [{:keys [fail error] :as r} (clojure.test/run-tests 'yang.clojure-callsite-test 'yang.core.call-test 'yin.vm.encoder-test)] (System/exit (if (zero? (+ fail error)) 0 1)))\"\nbb test:cljs   # Node lane for the same three namespaces\n```\n\nNo test result is claimed; the new pin and the existing `p1-packet-provenance-test` blocks should be confirmed green on JVM and Node before landing.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794210794000-engineer-cc1-p1-assoc-stale-metadata.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log:14:**Design choice:** the structural invariant, not an `assoc`-only patch. In [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:884), tracking metadata is now valid only for the exact vector object it was attached to. Every content-changing prelude primitive (`assoc`, `conj`, `vec`) routes its result through the single choke point `recover-rebuilt-packet` at [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:903), which drops `::origin-of` before lineage recovery. Extractive primitives (`first`, `get`) return the very tagged object, so they alone still trust its metadata. A rebuilt packet is re-provenanced only from its actual root/rows lineage; if no lineage entry accounts for it, it carries no provenance and is refused downstream as `:missing-provenance` rather than relabelled. In the repro, `(assoc a 0 (first b) 1 (first (rest b)))` now recovers `b`'s rows object from lineage and records the feed expansion's origin instead of `a`'s stale `[:source :program-in 0 0]`.\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794210794000-engineer-cc1-p1-assoc-stale-metadata.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log:32:clojure -M:test -e \"(require 'yang.clojure-callsite-test 'yang.core.call-test 'yin.vm.encoder-test) (let [{:keys [fail error] :as r} (clojure.test/run-tests 'yang.clojure-callsite-test 'yang.core.call-test 'yin.vm.encoder-test)] (System/exit (if (zero? (+ fail error)) 0 1)))\"\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794210254000-architect-cc1-p1-1-confirm.prompt.md:30:New pin: clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1096, your exact pick-second/feed/f repro,\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794210000000-architect-cc1-p1-confirm.findings.md:10:   (defmacro pick-second [a b]\ncollab/yang-clojure/1794210000000-architect-cc1-p1-confirm.findings.md:13:     (yin/application (yin/variable 'pick-second)\ncollab/yang-clojure/1