/0 (datagram green), and the FULL bb test:cljd 4508/0 — the float-address tests pass at true master too, so that \\\"pin debt\\\" item is CLOSED. (6) The kimi quality review was attempted but its sandbox wedge (static log); the seat answered the review questions from the tree (the module-spec docstring names call-address as the yang.call require address; the only call site; ordering proven by the passing gates) — ACCEPT; the fix landed as 578753c0 on fix/cljd-module-spec (pushed) and merged to master f7a9ae8f (pushed).\\norchestrator-logs/1793179048-yang-php-yang-typescript-glm-resume.md:717:Done: (1) G3 at true master (a717da28 lineage) is GREEN on all three lanes: JVM 4,887 tests / 303,186 assertions / 0 failures (the 3 latte items are the yang.clojure track's recorded BLOCKED gate, pre-existing); Dart cljd 4,508 / 0; Node cljs 4,608 / 158,495 / 0 failures. The earlier failure reports all traced to the stale-clone base (fixed, codified a717da28). (2) generators-v1: ALREADY ACTIVE at master — completed-steps carries :p4-s8 and the generator fixtures ran green inside the G3 consumer namespaces; kimi's checkpoint-B authorization was thus already exercised; no round needed. (3) The delegate-tooling corrections, owner-prompted: agy argon is quota-walled (~161h) but agy's OTHER models are live (claude-opus-5-5-high and gemini-3.8-flash-high probed real responses) — model-level routing recorded; my two flips on agy availability (out -> in -> intermittently-out -> model-level) both traced to trusting session-level errors over fresh probes. muse on shiva WORKS: the earlier \\\"cannot sandbox\\\" read was wrong — the headless invocation needed --trust-workspace (interactive muse trusts by itself; the owner verified by running muse interactively in ~/workspace/datomworld). The delegate-reference gains the flag in the muse recipe (ca6dd750, pushed). (4) The xlang slice-1 round (the shared conformance helper + the TS<->PHP legs, the postwalk rewrites deleted) runs on muse with