{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'ba2deb73|blob|gh api|api.github|sha|recover-rebuilt' collab/yang-clojure/1794210794000-engineer-cc1-p1-assoc-stale-metadata.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log; command -v git gh clojure; ls /opt/homebrew/bin/git; ls /tmp/cc1-p1/.cpcache\"","aggregated_output":"14:**Design choice:** the structural invariant, not an `assoc`-only patch. In [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:884), tracking metadata is now valid only for the exact vector object it was attached to. Every content-changing prelude primitive (`assoc`, `conj`, `vec`) routes its result through the single choke point `recover-rebuilt-packet` at [macro.cljc](/tmp/cc1-p1/src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc:903), which drops `::origin-of` before lineage recovery. Extractive primitives (`first`, `get`) return the very tagged object, so they alone still trust its metadata. A rebuilt packet is re-provenanced only from its actual root/rows lineage; if no lineage entry accounts for it, it carries no provenance and is refused downstream as `:missing-provenance` rather than relabelled. In the repro, `(assoc a 0 (first b) 1 (first (rest b)))` now recovers `b`'s rows object from lineage and records the feed expansion's origin instead of `a`'s stale `[:source :program-in 0 0]`.\n/usr/bin/git\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh\n/Users/sto/.local/share/mise/installs/clojure/1.12.4.1602/bin/clojure\nls: /opt/homebrew/bin/git: No such file or directory\nls: /tmp/cc1-p1/.cpcache: No such file or directory\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '710,1110p' src/cljc/yin/vm/macro.cljc; rg -n 'p1-packet|pick-second|assoc|subvec' test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc; cat deps.edn | head -n 100; cat .git\"","aggregated_output":"        (only-fn exact)\n        (only-fn (filter #(and (= (count (:rows %)) (count rows))\n                               (every? true?\n                                       (map identical? (:rows %) rows)))\n                         entries))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private missing-provenance-origin\n  \"The origin an unaccounted child answers below its coordinate: no\n   sanctioned operation threaded provenance to it, so nothing may\n   relabel its occurrences as this expansion's construction (P1-1).\n   `output-correspondence` carries the marker through and\n   `expand-call` refuses the output as `:missing-provenance`; the\n   marker never reaches a table, a row, or an event.\"\n  [:expansion ::missing])\n\n\n(defn- constructed-origin-fn\n  \"The origin function of a packet the prelude constructed: its root\n   occurrence carries the pending expansion origin; a relative path\n   below a child coordinate delegates to the packet passed for that\n   child — a spliced operand retains its own incoming origin, however\n   the macro's code embedded it. `recover` answers a child packet's\n   retained origin function when the packet itself carries none (it\n   was rebuilt by decomposition/reassembly); a child neither source\n   accounts for answers `missing-provenance-origin` below its\n   coordinate, which the expander refuses rather than reads as\n   construction.\"\n  ([coord-children] (constructed-origin-fn coord-children (fn [_] nil)))\n  ([coord-children recover]\n   (fn [rel]\n     (if (empty? rel)\n       pending-expansion-origin\n       (if-some [child (get coord-children (first rel))]\n         (if-some [f (or (origin-of-fn child) (recover child))]\n           (f (subvec rel 1))\n  